Subject: [PATCH] Molten Core: the Majordomo add holds also count for the AoE checks

WHY THIS PATCH EXISTS

Patches 0017 (casters hold off a Magic Reflection add) and 0018 (melee step
off a Damage Shield add) take effect only for the damage target exclusion
type. At the pinned fork revision the Aoe exclusion type is used in one place,
HasEnoughAoeTargets, which subtracts the excluded adds from the count of
attackers around a point. It never picks or aims a target. Its callers are
the generic AoE trigger (a "fire AoE" gate) and the channel checks (Blizzard,
Mind Sear, Hurricane and the Hunter and Warlock ones) that cancel a running
channel. Because the two holds did not fire for the Aoe type, a Flamewaker
Healer (11663) or Flamewaker Elite (11664) carrying Magic Reflection (20619)
or Damage Shield (21075) still counted for a caster's or a melee bot's AoE
trigger, so the bot kept area damage going into the pack. This is a
follow-up to patches 0017 and 0018 and builds on 0017 to 0020, which edit
the same function. The context of the hunk below deliberately spans the top
of the function (patch 0020) and the kill order block (patch 0019), so the
patch cannot apply to a tree that lacks them.

WHAT IT DOES

The caster hold and the melee step-off each accept the Aoe type as well as the
damage target type. Nothing else changes: the same bot class, the same aura
ids and the same two add entries, so the conditions are the ones the damage
target path already uses. A caster with a reflecting add, or a melee bot with
a Damage Shield add, in the pack sees a lower count for the AoE trigger and
the channel-cancel checks, so the trigger does not fire or a running channel
is cancelled sooner, and the bot falls back to its normal single-target
damage, which already leaves that add alone. The Aoe check of a tank never
gets here (the function returns early for it, see patch 0020), so every Aoe
check that does is a non-tank. The Majordomo and Core Rager exclusion already
applied to it and is unchanged. The kill order (patch 0019) stays on the
damage target type, and the tank block of patch 0020 is untouched.

The exclusions are recomputed on every call and a hold ends the moment the
aura drops, so a bot never stays on single-target damage for longer than the
aura lasts and cannot go idle because of this patch.

KNOWN COST

Ground-targeted or persistent area spells (Blizzard, Hurricane, Mind Sear)
may not be reflected by Magic Reflection, so cancelling them can lose some
damage. Melee Whirlwind and Cleave are physical and do take Damage Shield, so
that half is right.

WHAT THIS PATCH DELIBERATELY DOES NOT DO

It does not touch the kill order, the tank retake, the log line or the aura
ids, and it does not change how the fork picks targets. Nothing here was
compiled or run: the fork build is not available where this was written, and
a live Majordomo run confirms it.

WHEN THIS PATCH SHOULD BE DELETED

When the fork's Molten Core strategy applies the reflect hold and the Damage
Shield step-off to its AoE checks itself.

diff --git a/src/Ai/Raid/MC/MCStrategy.cpp b/src/Ai/Raid/MC/MCStrategy.cpp
index e23dc68..8d7fd21 100644
--- a/src/Ai/Raid/MC/MCStrategy.cpp
+++ b/src/Ai/Raid/MC/MCStrategy.cpp
@@ -111,121 +111,127 @@ void RaidMcStrategy::InitMultipliers(std::vector<Multiplier*>& multipliers)
 void RaidMcStrategy::AppendTargetExclusions(GuidSet& exclusions, TargetValueExclusionType type)
 {
     if (type == TargetValueExclusionType::Aoe && PlayerbotAI::IsTank(botAI->GetBot()))
         return;
 
     if (type == TargetValueExclusionType::TankTarget)
     {
         // Majordomo's Teleport Target throws his victim, the tank, into the
         // pit, and the Flamewaker adds it held turn on the raid. Tank target
         // selection takes its pick from what is left after these exclusions,
         // so while an add is attacking a player who is not a tank, Majordomo
         // himself and the adds a tank already holds are excluded. The tank
         // re-takes the loose add. With no loose add nothing is excluded and
         // tank selection is the stock one, so a tank is never left without a
         // target and never pulls Majordomo while an add is loose.
         AiObjectContext* context = botAI->GetAiObjectContext();
         bool looseAdd = false;
         for (ObjectGuid const guid : AI_VALUE(GuidVector, "attackers"))
         {
             Unit* unit = botAI->GetUnit(guid);
             Unit* victim = unit ? unit->GetVictim() : nullptr;
             Player* victimPlayer = victim ? victim->ToPlayer() : nullptr;
             if (unit && (unit->GetEntry() == NPC_FLAMEWAKER_HEALER || unit->GetEntry() == NPC_FLAMEWAKER_ELITE) &&
                 victimPlayer && !PlayerbotAI::IsTank(victimPlayer))
             {
                 looseAdd = true;
                 break;
             }
         }
         if (looseAdd)
         {
             for (ObjectGuid const guid : AI_VALUE(GuidVector, "attackers"))
             {
                 Unit* unit = botAI->GetUnit(guid);
                 if (!unit)
                     continue;
 
                 Unit* victim = unit->GetVictim();
                 Player* victimPlayer = victim ? victim->ToPlayer() : nullptr;
                 if (unit->GetEntry() == NPC_MAJORDOMO_EXECUTUS ||
                     ((unit->GetEntry() == NPC_FLAMEWAKER_HEALER || unit->GetEntry() == NPC_FLAMEWAKER_ELITE) &&
                      victimPlayer && PlayerbotAI::IsTank(victimPlayer)))
                     exclusions.insert(guid);
             }
         }
         return;
     }
 
     // Damage into these is wasted: Core Ragers are unkillable while Golemagg
     // lives (full heal at 50%), and Majordomo reflects and cannot die; his
     // encounter ends when the eight adds are dead. Tanks still pick them up
     // through their own target selection.
     AiObjectContext* context = botAI->GetAiObjectContext();
     bool const golemaggAlive = AI_VALUE2(Unit*, "find target", "golemagg the incinerator") != nullptr;
     // Magic Reflection returns a caster's own spell to the caster. Casters
     // leave a reflecting add alone: they take another add that is not
     // reflecting, or they have no target and wait until the aura drops.
     Player* bot = botAI->GetBot();
-    bool const casterHolds = type == TargetValueExclusionType::DpsTarget && PlayerbotAI::IsCaster(bot);
+    // The Aoe type is only counted here for a bot that is not a tank: a held
+    // add then no longer counts toward its AoE trigger and channel checks.
+    bool const casterHolds =
+        (type == TargetValueExclusionType::DpsTarget || type == TargetValueExclusionType::Aoe) &&
+        PlayerbotAI::IsCaster(bot);
     Unit* reflecting = nullptr;
     // Damage Shield hurts every melee swing into its holder. Melee step off
     // an add that carries it and take another add, or wait until it drops.
-    bool const meleeStepsOff = type == TargetValueExclusionType::DpsTarget && PlayerbotAI::IsMelee(bot);
+    bool const meleeStepsOff =
+        (type == TargetValueExclusionType::DpsTarget || type == TargetValueExclusionType::Aoe) &&
+        PlayerbotAI::IsMelee(bot);
     for (ObjectGuid const guid : AI_VALUE(GuidVector, "attackers"))
     {
         Unit* unit = botAI->GetUnit(guid);
         if (!unit)
             continue;
 
         if ((golemaggAlive && unit->GetEntry() == NPC_CORE_RAGER) || unit->GetEntry() == NPC_MAJORDOMO_EXECUTUS)
             exclusions.insert(guid);
         else if (casterHolds && unit->HasAura(SPELL_MAGIC_REFLECTION) &&
                  (unit->GetEntry() == NPC_FLAMEWAKER_HEALER || unit->GetEntry() == NPC_FLAMEWAKER_ELITE))
         {
             exclusions.insert(guid);
             reflecting = unit;
         }
         else if (meleeStepsOff && unit->HasAura(SPELL_DAMAGE_REFLECTION) &&
                  (unit->GetEntry() == NPC_FLAMEWAKER_HEALER || unit->GetEntry() == NPC_FLAMEWAKER_ELITE))
             exclusions.insert(guid);
     }
 
     // Kill order: the Flamewaker Healers die first, the Elites after. While a
     // healer is alive, this bot can see it, and it is not itself excluded
     // above, the Elites are left alone. A healer that is excluded, out of
     // spell range, out of line of sight, dead or immune does not count (the
     // attackers list holds only valid targets), so the Elites are open to
     // the bot again and it never waits on a healer it cannot reach.
     bool const healersFirst = type == TargetValueExclusionType::DpsTarget;
     bool healerInReach = false;
     if (healersFirst)
     {
         for (ObjectGuid const guid : AI_VALUE(GuidVector, "attackers"))
         {
             Unit* unit = botAI->GetUnit(guid);
             if (unit && unit->GetEntry() == NPC_FLAMEWAKER_HEALER && exclusions.find(guid) == exclusions.end() &&
                 bot->GetDistance(unit) <= sPlayerbotAIConfig.SpellDistance && bot->IsWithinLOSInMap(unit))
             {
                 healerInReach = true;
                 break;
             }
         }
     }
     if (healerInReach)
     {
         for (ObjectGuid const guid : AI_VALUE(GuidVector, "attackers"))
         {
             Unit* unit = botAI->GetUnit(guid);
             if (unit && unit->GetEntry() == NPC_FLAMEWAKER_ELITE)
                 exclusions.insert(guid);
         }
     }
 
     if (reflecting)
     {
         // Casters that held in the last three seconds, counted across the
         // raid, and one line per three seconds, not one per bot per tick.
         static std::mutex holdMutex;
         static std::unordered_map<ObjectGuid, uint32> heldAtMs;
         static uint32 lastLogMs = 0;
         uint32 const nowMs = getMSTime();
